 * list, rendered via a groupSize={10}-chunked, position-locked layout.
 * Dropped both, per Cathal directly: he no longer needs the full list's
 * exact order/pairing preserved — only his strongest images need to stay
 * pinned at the top of the page. PORTRAITS_ORDER is now just that: a
 * priority list. applyOrder() still puts every listed filename first, in
 * the order given, but PhotoMasonry no longer tries to force any of them
 * (or the auto-appended rest) into specific columns — the whole
 * collection now flows through ONE continuous height-balanced masonry
 * (distributeColumns() in photography.ts, no groupSize), so it looks
 * like genuine masonry — including for photos never explicitly ordered
 * — instead of fighting the algorithm to preserve a hand-picked layout.
 * A small chunked group (see groupSize's own note) simply doesn't have
 * enough photos for height-balancing to work well; the full ~177-photo
 * archive does. New drop-in files still just work — no code changes
 * needed, they auto-append after the curated portion via applyOrder().
 */
